From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mini: order publication and consumption of delegate trampoline caches.

The Ampere ARM64 build of Wine-Mono 11.3.0 crashes in Roslyn while compiling
mscorlib.dll. The saved core contains an Action for CompileNamedTypeAsync
with the optimized invoke_impl but a NULL method_ptr. The shared
MonoDelegateTrampInfo already contains both valid pointers. The ARM64
invoke stub loads method_ptr and branches to zero.

mono_delegate_trampoline publishes method_ptr followed by invoke_impl,
and the inlined constructor reads invoke_impl followed by method_ptr.
Neither side orders those accesses. On weakly ordered CPUs a constructor
can therefore copy the new invoke_impl together with the old NULL
method_ptr, permanently skipping lazy initialization for that delegate.

Publish the target before the optimized entry point with a write barrier,
and acquire the entry point before reading the target in the generated
constructor. Keep the invoke_impl-first read order: observing the old lazy
entry with a new target is safe, but the inverse is not. Also order the
target before publishing the optimized entry on the delegate itself.

This fixes the runtime protocol rather than disabling Roslyn parallelism
or changing the compiler or class-library profile. The existing prep loop
applies it to both the native host Mono and the Windows runtime builds.
---
diff --git a/mono/mini/mini-trampolines.c b/mono/mini/mini-trampolines.c
--- a/mono/mini/mini-trampolines.c
+++ b/mono/mini/mini-trampolines.c
@@ -1221,9 +1221,13 @@ mono_delegate_trampoline (host_mgreg_t *regs, guint8 *code, gpointer *arg, guint8* tramp)
 		code = (guint8 *)mini_add_method_trampoline (m, code, mono_method_needs_static_rgctx_invoke (m, FALSE), FALSE);
 	}
 
+	/* The optimized entry point uses method_ptr without lazy initialization. */
+	mono_memory_write_barrier ();
 	delegate->invoke_impl = mono_get_addr_from_ftnptr (code);
 	if (enable_caching && !callvirt && tramp_info->method) {
 		tramp_info->method_ptr = delegate->method_ptr;
+		/* Pair with the acquire in the inlined delegate constructor. */
+		mono_memory_write_barrier ();
 		tramp_info->invoke_impl = delegate->invoke_impl;
 	}
 
diff --git a/mono/mini/method-to-ir.c b/mono/mini/method-to-ir.c
--- a/mono/mini/method-to-ir.c
+++ b/mono/mini/method-to-ir.c
@@ -3699,6 +3699,8 @@ handle_delegate_ctor (MonoCompile *cfg, MonoClass *klass, MonoInst *target, MonoMethod *method, int target_method_context_used, int invoke_context_used, gboolean virtual_)
 	} else {
 		dreg = alloc_preg (cfg);
 		MONO_EMIT_NEW_LOAD_MEMBASE (cfg, dreg, tramp_ins->dreg, MONO_STRUCT_OFFSET (MonoDelegateTrampInfo, invoke_impl));
+		/* A cached optimized entry must not be paired with a stale method_ptr. */
+		mini_emit_memory_barrier (cfg, MONO_MEMORY_BARRIER_ACQ);
 		MONO_EMIT_NEW_STORE_MEMBASE (cfg, OP_STORE_MEMBASE_REG, obj->dreg, MONO_STRUCT_OFFSET (MonoDelegate, invoke_impl), dreg);
 
 		dreg = alloc_preg (cfg);
